    "Model Selection Rationale: The task is MNIST-style handwritten digit classification on a CPU-only system with a strict runtime memory cap and latency target. Mobilenet_v2 offers the best practical balance among common lightweight architectures: very low memory usage, fast CPU inference, and sufficient capacity for MNIST with proper training. ResNet-50, while capable, is heavier and may approach or exceed latency/memory targets on typical CPUs; it remains a viable fallback if a modestly higher accuracy or specific transfer-learning setup is required. Other candidates (e.g., mobilenet_v3_small, efficientnet_b0) are also feasible, but mobilenet_v2 generally provides a robust baseline with simpler deployment. If latency becomes an issue, consider a smaller variant or quantization.",
